---
export const title = 'Views';
export const order = 200;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  Each entry of <code>available-views</code> is <code>&#123; value, label?, slot, days? &#125;</code>.
  <code>slot</code> is what a column stands for: <code>hour</code> or <code>day</code>. Without <code>days</code>, the
  view is a calendar month, and a view whose <code>value</code> is <code>week</code> starts on the week's first day.
  The defaults are <code>day</code> (24 hour columns), <code>week</code> (7 day columns) and <code>month</code>.
</p>

<p>
  In hour views an event is drawn from its start to its end, and drags snap to <code>minute-step</code> minutes. In day
  views an event covers the days it touches and shows its start time, and drags move it by whole days, keeping its
  times. Events that overlap in a row stack in lanes. Columns share the width but are never narrower than
  <code>--timeline-grid-hour-width</code> (4rem) or <code>--timeline-grid-day-width</code> (3rem); a range that does
  not fit scrolls sideways, under a header and a resource column that stay in place. Today is tinted and weekends are
  shaded in day views, and a line marks the current time.
</p>

<p>
  The header, <code>date</code>, <code>contextDate</code>, <code>view</code>, <code>first-day</code>,
  <code>timezone</code>, <code>locale</code>, <code>previous()</code>, <code>next()</code>, <code>today()</code>,
  <code>date-change</code> and <code>view-change</code> work as in <code>wc-calendar</code>, so the two can share a
  view switcher and a date.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-timeline-grid id='team-grid' view='week' resource-label='People' style='height: 360px; width: 100%'></wc-timeline-grid>
  <script is:inline>
    (function() {
      const $grid = document.getElementById('team-grid');

      $grid.availableViews = [
        { value: 'day', slot: 'hour', days: 1 },
        { value: 'week', slot: 'day', days: 7 },
        { value: 'week-hours', label: 'Week by hour', slot: 'hour', days: 7 },
        { value: 'month', slot: 'day' },
      ];

      const today = new Date();
      today.setHours(0, 0, 0, 0);

      function day(offset, hours) {
        const result = new Date(today);
        result.setDate(result.getDate() + offset);
        result.setHours(hours || 0, 0, 0, 0);
        return result;
      }

      $grid.resources = [
        { id: 'priya', title: 'Priya Natarajan', supportingText: 'Design' },
        { id: 'tomas', title: 'Tomás Ruiz', supportingText: 'Engineering' },
        { id: 'mei', title: 'Mei Chen', supportingText: 'Support' },
      ];

      $grid.events = [
        { resourceId: 'priya', title: 'Workshop', start: day(-1, 9), end: day(-1, 17), color: 'blue' },
        { resourceId: 'priya', title: 'Leave', start: day(2), end: day(4), color: 'orange' },
        { resourceId: 'tomas', title: 'On call', start: day(0), end: day(3), color: 'red' },
        { resourceId: 'mei', title: 'Early shift', start: day(0, 6), end: day(0, 14), color: 'green' },
        { resourceId: 'mei', title: 'Early shift', start: day(1, 6), end: day(1, 14), color: 'green' },
      ];
    })();
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>
